<main id="main"><header class="page-hero container"><span class="section-label">YOUR INFORMATION</span><h1>Privacy policy.</h1><p>What the website uses, and what it does not store. Last updated: 17 November 2026.</p></header><div class="article-shell container"><aside class="article-aside">Site policies</aside><article class="article-body">
<h2>1. What we do</h2><p><?= esc(SITE_NAME) ?> provides an internet speed test and guides about network performance. During a test, your browser transfers temporary test data to and from our server to estimate download, upload, ping and jitter.</p>
<h2>2. Technical connection information</h2><p>Our hosting server receives ordinary technical request information such as your public IP address, time of request, browser and volume transferred. The hosting provider may retain standard access or security logs. We do not require a user account or maintain a website history of your finished tests.</p>
<h2>3. Network provider lookup</h2><p>On the home page, LineSpeed may use <a href="https://ipinfo.io" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">IPinfo</a> to look up public IP network ownership (ASN and approximate provider name) and country. This requires sharing your public IP address with that service, which processes it under its own terms and privacy policy. The provider shown is an estimate: it may reflect a VPN, an upstream network or other infrastructure, not the brand on your bill.</p>
<h2>4. Cookies and local preferences</h2><p>We use a temporary, first-party PHP session cookie to protect high-bandwidth testing endpoints. Your browser can also store your selected language and light/dark appearance using localStorage. These preferences are not advertising trackers. Clearing your browser's site data resets them. The network lookup result may be cached briefly in the server session to avoid repeated external requests.</p>
<h2>5. Uploaded test data and result pictures</h2><p>We generate random upload test data in your browser. The server reads it and discards it rather than saving it as an uploaded file. When you choose to save a PNG report, your browser generates and downloads the image to your device; we do not store the report on our server.</p>
<h2>6. External fonts and hosting</h2><p>We use Google Fonts to display Poppins. Your browser may make requests to Google to load fonts. Our hosting provider may process standard technical logs needed to deliver the website.</p>
<h2>7. Advertising and analytics</h2><p><strong>There are no AdSense advertising tags or third-party analytics trackers in this starter website.</strong> If we introduce ads or analytics, we must update this notice and set up the disclosures and consent required by applicable laws and Google's policies before enabling those services. In particular, serving personalised ads to users in the EEA, UK or Switzerland requires a suitable Google-certified consent management platform.</p>
<h2>8. Contact</h2><p>To ask about this policy or make a privacy request, please use our <a href="/contact.php">contact page</a>. The publisher must provide a valid email address before public launch.</p>
